Subject: [PATCH 06981/11362] Task 9 A/B: InertClickSigPruner matched-budget
 measurement -- zero regression, honest no-op at tested budget
 (REQ-ARC-FCP-5595-2)

Extends scripts/arc_loop_solve.py's solve_adaptered with a new
inert_click_prune bool param, composing InertClickSigPruner into the same
move_pruner construction hazard_prune/mask_prune already use -- mirrors
HazardMovePruner's own tu93 A/B precedent exactly (OfflineSolver, states_
expanded, the offline reproduction gate as correctness backstop).

Ran the real A/B on m0r0 (target_level=2, hazard_prune/mask_prune fixed
False in both arms): baseline and treatment both reach L2, both pass
offline_reproduced=True, states_expanded identical (38 vs 38) --
pruner_stats shows observed=0 (the directed, verifier-guided search never
even attempts a repeated click on this specific level range, unlike broad
exploration).

Added an independent live-wired supplementary check: a real E3AgentPolicy
construction with inert_click_pruner=True from the start, confirming the
wiring engages during live exploration -- 32 clicks observed, 0 pruned
(consistent with exp5595's own original finding: evidence never clears the
min_observations=4 floor within this budget).

honest_verdict=complete: inert_click_pruner_ab_no_op_offline_and_live_at_
this_budget_on_m0r0. Zero regression confirmed across 3 independent checks
(exp5595, this OfflineSolver A/B, this live-wired check) -- recommendation:
do NOT flip SUBMITTED_INERT_CLICK_PRUNER_ENABLED yet; no measured benefit at
tested budgets, though also no measured harm.

REQ-ARC-FCP-5595-2 + SCENARIO-ARC-FCP-5595-2-MATCHED-BUDGET-AB added to
spec.md. 7 new tests; 22 related tests pass.

